export const modernPerspective = [
  'Dynamical stability is a Brillouin-zone statement. A stable Γ-point calculation does not exclude a finite-q soft mode, and a high-symmetry path does not sample every possible instability. The relevant q-space coverage has to match the stability claim being made.',
  'A negative harmonic eigenvalue diagnoses negative local curvature of the chosen Born–Oppenheimer energy surface. It does not by itself determine the finite-temperature phase: anharmonicity, entropy, competing structures, quantum nuclear motion, and the exchange–correlation model can all change the thermodynamic problem.',
  'Electron–phonon coupling adds convergence requirements beyond an ordinary phonon calculation because Fermi-surface phase space and k↔k+q matrix elements must be resolved together. A converged phonon dispersion therefore does not establish convergence of g, α²F(ω), λ, or a superconducting transition temperature inferred from them.',
